.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/d3-ease Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "d3-ease"
.PP
\fIEasing\fP is a method of distorting time to control apparent motion in animation\&. It is most commonly used for \fRslow-in, slow-out\fP\&. By easing time, \fRanimated transitions\fP are smoother and exhibit more plausible motion\&.

.PP
The easing types in this module implement the \fBease method\fP, which takes a normalized time \fIt\fP and returns the corresponding “eased” time \fItʹ\fP\&. Both the normalized time and the eased time are typically in the range [0,1], where 0 represents the start of the animation and 1 represents the end; some easing types, such as \fBelastic\fP, may return eased times slightly outside this range\&. A good easing type should return 0 if \fIt\fP = 0 and 1 if \fIt\fP = 1\&. See the \fReasing explorer\fP for a visual demonstration\&.

.PP
These easing types are largely based on work by \fRRobert Penner\fP\&.
.SH "Installing"
.PP
If you use npm, \fRnpm install d3-ease\fP\&. You can also download the \fRlatest release on GitHub\fP\&. For vanilla HTML in modern browsers, import d3-ease from Skypack:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script type="module">

import {easeCubic} from "https://cdn\&.skypack\&.dev/d3\-ease@3";

const e = easeCubic(0\&.25);

</script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
For legacy environments, you can load d3-ease’s UMD bundle from an npm-based CDN such as jsDelivr; a \fRd3\fP global is exported:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<script src="https://cdn\&.jsdelivr\&.net/npm/d3\-ease@3"></script>
<script>

const e = d3\&.easeCubic(0\&.25);

</script>
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fRTry d3-ease in your browser\&.\fP
.SH "API Reference"
.PP
# \fIease\fP(\fIt\fP)

.PP
Given the specified normalized time \fIt\fP, typically in the range [0,1], returns the “eased” time \fItʹ\fP, also typically in [0,1]\&. 0 represents the start of the animation and 1 represents the end\&. A good implementation returns 0 if \fIt\fP = 0 and 1 if \fIt\fP = 1\&. See the \fReasing explorer\fP for a visual demonstration\&. For example, to apply \fBcubic\fP easing:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const te = d3\&.easeCubic(t);
.fi
.PP

.PP
Similarly, to apply custom \fBelastic\fP easing:

.PP
.PP
.nf
// Before the animation starts, create your easing function\&.
const customElastic = d3\&.easeElastic\&.period(0\&.4);

// During the animation, apply the easing function\&.
const te = customElastic(t);
.fi
.PP

.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseLinear\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Linear easing; the identity function; \fIlinear\fP(\fIt\fP) returns \fIt\fP\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeasePolyIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Polynomial easing; raises \fIt\fP to the specified \fBexponent\fP\&. If the exponent is not specified, it defaults to 3, equivalent to \fBcubicIn\fP\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeasePolyOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse polynomial easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBpolyIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&. If the \fBexponent\fP is not specified, it defaults to 3, equivalent to \fBcubicOut\fP\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeasePoly\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeasePolyInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric polynomial easing; scales \fBpolyIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBpolyOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&. If the \fBexponent\fP is not specified, it defaults to 3, equivalent to \fBcubic\fP\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# \fIpoly\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(\fIe\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Returns a new polynomial easing with the specified exponent \fIe\fP\&. For example, to create equivalents of \fBlinear\fP, \fBquad\fP, and \fBcubic\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const linear = d3\&.easePoly\&.exponent(1);
const quad = d3\&.easePoly\&.exponent(2);
const cubic = d3\&.easePoly\&.exponent(3);
.fi
.PP

.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseQuadIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Quadratic easing; equivalent to \fBpolyIn\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(2)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseQuadOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse quadratic easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBquadIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&. Also equivalent to \fBpolyOut\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(2)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseQuad\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseQuadInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric quadratic easing; scales \fBquadIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBquadOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&. Also equivalent to \fBpoly\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(2)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCubicIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Cubic easing; equivalent to \fBpolyIn\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(3)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCubicOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse cubic easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBcubicIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&. Also equivalent to \fBpolyOut\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(3)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCubic\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseCubicInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric cubic easing; scales \fBcubicIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBcubicOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&. Also equivalent to \fBpoly\fP\&.\fBexponent\fP(3)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseSinIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Sinusoidal easing; returns sin(\fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseSinOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse sinusoidal easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBsinIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseSin\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseSinInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric sinusoidal easing; scales \fBsinIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBsinOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseExpIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Exponential easing; raises 2 to the exponent 10 * (\fIt\fP - 1)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseExpOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse exponential easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBexpIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseExp\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseExpInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric exponential easing; scales \fBexpIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBexpOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCircleIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Circular easing\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCircleOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse circular easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBcircleIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseCircle\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseCircleInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric circular easing; scales \fBcircleIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBcircleOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseElasticIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Elastic easing, like a rubber band\&. The \fBamplitude\fP and \fBperiod\fP of the oscillation are configurable; if not specified, they default to 1 and 0\&.3, respectively\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseElastic\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseElasticOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse elastic easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBelasticIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseElasticInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric elastic easing; scales \fBelasticIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBelasticOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# \fIelastic\fP\&.\fBamplitude\fP(\fIa\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Returns a new elastic easing with the specified amplitude \fIa\fP\&.

.PP
# \fIelastic\fP\&.\fBperiod\fP(\fIp\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Returns a new elastic easing with the specified period \fIp\fP\&.

.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBackIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
\fRAnticipatory\fP easing, like a dancer bending his knees before jumping off the floor\&. The degree of \fBovershoot\fP is configurable; if not specified, it defaults to 1\&.70158\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBackOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse anticipatory easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBbackIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBack\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseBackInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric anticipatory easing; scales \fBbackIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBbackOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# \fIback\fP\&.\fBovershoot\fP(\fIs\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Returns a new back easing with the specified overshoot \fIs\fP\&.

.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBounceIn\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Bounce easing, like a rubber ball\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBounce\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP 
.br
# d3\&.\fBeaseBounceOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Reverse bounce easing; equivalent to 1 - \fBbounceIn\fP(1 - \fIt\fP)\&.

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
# d3\&.\fBeaseBounceInOut\fP(\fIt\fP) \fR<>\fP

.PP
Symmetric bounce easing; scales \fBbounceIn\fP for \fIt\fP in [0, 0\&.5] and \fBbounceOut\fP for \fIt\fP in [0\&.5, 1]\&.

.PP
\fR\fP 
